From bdea22dbe757a47113ed8076c3c0ebf3e643a606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 079/145] media: meson: vdec: only parse MPEG1/2 sequence
 headers

The driver-side sequence-header parse that supplies the initial
SOURCE_CHANGE for codecs whose firmware raises no header interrupt is
gated on the absence of a .resume op.  That was accurate when MPEG1/2
was the only such codec, but it is the wrong predicate: it selects "no
resume op", when what the parser actually requires is "this is an
MPEG1/2 stream".

vdec_parse_mpeg_seq_header() scans for the MPEG1/2 sequence header start
code 00 00 01 B3 and reads the next three bytes as a 12-bit width and
height.  MPEG-4 Part 2 uses that identical start code for
group_of_vop_start_code, where the following bytes are a time code.
Parsing them yields a nonsense coded size - 1x7 for the stream this was
found with.

The consequence is not a cosmetic one.  sess->width/height feed
amvdec_set_canvases(), so the capture canvases are built for the bogus
size while the microcode still decodes a full-size picture into them.
The decode runs off the end of every canvas: a wild bus-master write
that takes out the DDR controller, with no oops and nothing on the
console - only a physical reset recovers the board.

Nothing hits this today because MPEG1/2 is the only codec without a
resume op, so this is a latent trap rather than a live bug: it arms
itself for whoever adds the next such codec.  Gate on the pixel format
instead.

Found while bringing up MPEG-4 Part 2 on this driver, which wedged the
SoC twice before the cause was traced with a serial console.
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
index 1240be46959d..b8c73703fdda 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -340,9 +340,21 @@ static void vdec_vb2_buf_queue(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 
 	v4l2_m2m_buf_queue(m2m_ctx, vbuf);
 
+	/*
+	 * Only MPEG1/2 may take this path.  The parser below looks for the
+	 * MPEG1/2 sequence header 00 00 01 B3 - but MPEG-4 Part 2 uses that
+	 * very start code for group_of_vop, whose following bytes are a time
+	 * code, not a size.  Parsing it yields a nonsense resolution, the
+	 * canvases are then built for that size, and the microcode decodes a
+	 * full-size picture straight past the end of them: a wild DMA that
+	 * wedges the DDR controller.  Gate on the codec, not on the absence
+	 * of a resume op.
+	 */
 	if (vb->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE &&
 	    !sess->fmt_out->codec_ops->resume &&
-	    !sess->init_src_change_done)
+	    !sess->init_src_change_done &&
+	    (sess->fmt_out->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG1 ||
+	     sess->fmt_out->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2))
 		vdec_init_src_change(sess, vb);
 
 	if (!sess->streamon_out)
